#: src/dialogs.c:1340
msgid "By content, when you open a file"
msgstr "By what's inside, when ye open a crate"

#: src/dialogs.c:1343
msgid ""
"Other file managers go by the name: a “holiday.jpg” that is really a program "
"shows as a picture and opens in the picture viewer. By content, millerX also "
"reads the first few KB of a file when you select or open it, and where the "
"content says something else (a program, text, a picture, an archive), the "
"content wins: preview, Properties and the program that opens it. The icons "
"in the lists stay by name. Not a virus scanner: it catches files in "
"disguise, not every trick."
msgstr ""
"Other ships judge cargo by the label: a “holiday.jpg” that's really a cannon "
"looks like a picture and opens in the picture viewer. By what's inside, "
"millerX also peeks at the first few KB of a crate when ye pick or open it, "
"and where the inside says somethin' else (a cannon, words, a picture, a "
"chest), the inside wins: the peek, the crate's papers and who opens it. The "
"flags in the lists stay by label. It ain't no ship's doctor for plagues: it "
"catches cargo in disguise, not every trick."

